<%# ── FAQ ── %>
<section class="lp-block" id="faq" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="lp-shell">
    <div class="lp-section-head">
      <div class="lp-section-eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="lp-section-title">Common questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="lp-faq" data-controller="lp-faq">
      <div class="lp-faq-item lp-open" data-lp-faq-target="item">
        <button class="lp-faq-q" data-action="click->lp-faq#toggle" aria-expanded="true">
          <span>Is my data used to train AI models?</span>
          <%= plus_svg %>
        </button>
        <div class="lp-faq-a">
          <p>No. We use OpenAI's enterprise endpoints with zero data retention. Your documents are stored only in our database (encrypted at rest), and we never share them with any model provider for training.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-faq-item" data-lp-faq-target="item">
        <button class="lp-faq-q" data-action="click->lp-faq#toggle" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What if InternalQ doesn't know the answer?</span>
          <%= plus_svg %>
        </button>
        <div class="lp-faq-a">
          <p>It says so — explicitly. Every "I don't know" is logged so admins can see the gaps in their documentation and fill them. We'd rather say nothing than make something up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-faq-item" data-lp-faq-target="item">
        <button class="lp-faq-q" data-action="click->lp-faq#toggle" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Is InternalQ on the Slack Marketplace?</span>
          <%= plus_svg %>
        </button>
        <div class="lp-faq-a">
          <p>Our marketplace listing is currently under review by Slack. In the meantime, you can install InternalQ directly via OAuth — it's the same install flow you'd use from the marketplace, and your workspace owner approves it the same way.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-faq-item" data-lp-faq-target="item">
        <button class="lp-faq-q" data-action="click->lp-faq#toggle" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Can different teams have different document sets?</span>
          <%= plus_svg %>
        </button>
        <div class="lp-faq-a">
          <p>Yes. You can scope a document collection to specific Slack channels — engineering runbooks live in #engineering, HR policies live in #people-ops, and never the twain shall meet.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-faq-item" data-lp-faq-target="item">
        <button class="lp-faq-q" data-action="click->lp-faq#toggle" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What file types are supported?</span>
          <%= plus_svg %>
        </button>
        <div class="lp-faq-a">
          <p>PDF, DOCX, Markdown, and plain text up to 10 MB per file. We're adding Notion, Google Docs, and Confluence integrations next quarter.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lp-faq-item" data-lp-faq-target="item">
        <button class="lp-faq-q" data-action="click->lp-faq#toggle" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How much does it cost?</span>
          <%= plus_svg %>
        </button>
        <div class="lp-faq-a">
          <p>Free for 14 days, no credit card. After that, plans start at $39/month for teams up to 25 people. Larger teams: <%= link_to "see the pricing page", pricing_path %>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# ── Final CTA ── %>
<section class="lp-block" style="padding-top:24px;padding-bottom:0">
